+/**
+ * prescriptions list — tenant-isolation RED oracle (EHAC-1986 REPRO-01 → Phase 2).
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS PROVES (app-layer contract — Landmine B): the Phase-2 fix scopes the
+ * prescriptions report by emitting a roster-membership predicate into the AQL —
+ * `… n/items[at0006]/value matches { '<roster id>', … }` — on the stable
+ * `Patient_id` column that 02-03 ADDS to both report SELECT branches (the sibling
+ * getPrescriptionByEncounterIdOnly proves items[at0006] on the encounter_id cluster
+ * is the patient id). The roster is fetched from the org-scoped Demographics
+ * `searchPatients` (mirroring the patient list; demography.ts:36-42 +
+ * PatientList.tsx:183 — Key Decision #2). This oracle simulates the openEHR server
+ * applying that predicate: a canned, mixed-tenant row SURVIVES iff its `Patient_id`
+ * value appears as a single-quoted literal in the EMITTED AQL string.
+ *
+ * WHY THE ORACLE NOW KEYS ON `Patient_id`, NOT `Patient_name`: the spec controls its
+ * own canned rows, so it can key on the stable `Patient_id` (n/items[at0006]) that
+ * Phase 2 (02-03) adds — regardless of the current production SELECT — which removes
+ * the non-unique-name fragility of the Phase-1 oracle. 02-03 owns the column addition.
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE: a mocked `executeRaw` runs no AQL engine — it proves only
+ * that the APP emits a roster-scoped query, not that the openEHR SERVER scopes the
+ * rows. Server-side scoping is confirmed separately by the Playwright E2E.
+ *
+ * This spec deliberately does NOT mock `@ehacare/bettercare-sdk`, so the REAL
+ * `validateAQLQuery` runs (createPrescriptionAQLFilter calls it). validateAQLQuery is
+ * a PURE function (validation.ts:119-151 — string keyword/regex checks + logger.error
+ * only; no network/config/env/process side effects), so running it unmocked adds no
+ * infrastructure dependency and the spec fails on the roster oracle, not on infra.
+ *
+ * DO NOT make this green here — the fix is Phase 2's job (EHAC-1986, 02-03). This
+ * oracle is expected to be RED until then — pre-fix the prescription AQL has neither
+ * the Patient_id column nor the roster clause, so every canned row drops and the
+ * owned-survives / emitted-AQL assertions FAIL.
+ */
+
